#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'
Knowledge Hub Interactive Lab
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Kubernetes: ConfigMap Rollout

Scenario
  A Deployment reads APP_MESSAGE from a ConfigMap, but the value is stale.
  Updating the ConfigMap alone does not change the environment of an existing Pod.

Goal
  1. Inspect the ConfigMap and running Pod.
  2. Change APP_MESSAGE to: production-ready
  3. Apply the ConfigMap.
  4. Roll the Deployment so the new Pod receives the corrected value.

Start here
  status
  kubectl get configmap kh-config -n kh-lab -o yaml
  kubectl exec -n kh-lab deploy/kh-demo -- printenv APP_MESSAGE
  nano configmap.yaml

Lab commands
  status   inspect cluster state
  check    validate ConfigMap + live Pod state
  hint     reveal progressive help
  apply    apply configmap.yaml and restart the Deployment
  reset    restore the broken scenario
  help     show this assignment again
EOF
